New cleric skill: rites.

1) Rites draws what is left of a soul into a soulstone.
   - You must be seated, holding your holy symbol, with holy water to hand
     and a soulstone to catch what comes.

2) The body must be whole.
   - Skinned, butchered or dissected, it has already been opened and there
     is nothing left to call.

3) What a stone takes is its own level against a tenth of the corpse's.
   - Your own level never enters it.
   - Your skill decides whether the words land, never how much they yield.

4) A body the rites have been said over is finished.
   - Nothing else can be taken from it, and it cannot be sacrificed.

See HELP RITES and HELP SOULSTONE.
